<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Ouetsu Reppan Domei</h1><p class="st-meta">1868 CE – 1868 CE · capital Shiroishi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The alliance of some thirty northern domains formed in 1868 to resist the new Meiji government, the largest opposition in the Boshin War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a>'s defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-toba-fushimi">Toba-Fushimi</a>, the new government ordered northern domains to punish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aizu">Aizu</a> and Shonai. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sendai">Sendai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yonezawa">Yonezawa</a> sought pardon for them, and when this was refused, delegates met at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiroishi-miyagi">Shiroishi</a> in May 1868 and formed an alliance, joined by Nagaoka and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/echigo-province">Echigo</a> domains.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The alliance was a council of member domains rather than a state, with headquarters at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiroishi-miyagi">Shiroishi</a> and leadership from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sendai">Sendai</a>. It invited Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-kitashirakawa-yoshihisa">Rinnoji-no-miya Yoshihisa</a>, a member of the imperial family who had fled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-tokyo">Edo</a>, to serve as its nominal head, presenting itself as loyal to the throne but opposed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satsuma-domain">Satsuma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/choshu-domain">Choshu</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Kubota and others defected, Nagaoka fell, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yonezawa">Yonezawa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sendai">Sendai</a> surrendered in October 1868, followed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aizu">Aizu</a> and Shonai in November. Some alliance fighters joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-ezo">Republic of Ezo</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/ouetsu-reppan-domei.jpg" alt="Ouetsu Reppan Domei" width="320" height="484"><figcaption>Image: Amcaja · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Standard-bearer_in_2006_Aizu_parade.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1868 CE – 1868 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Shiroishi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Rinnoji-no-miya Yoshihisa, Date Yoshikuni</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, Shinto</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Japanese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/japan">Japan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Northern Alliance, Alliance of the Northern Domains, Ou-Etsu Reppan Domei</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1868&amp;focus=ouetsu-reppan-domei" aria-label="Ouetsu Reppan Domei on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="8184 812 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ouetsu Reppan Domei lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M8504 1068L8505 1059M8504 1068L8529 1145"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8505 1059h0M8529 1145h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8504 1068h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8504 1068h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Shiroishi. <a href="/atlas?year=1868&amp;focus=ouetsu-reppan-domei">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

